# Panels in windows of their own (Member Request from Richard Throgmorton (MakIt3D), Founding Member #1) for the look
# review at 1440 logical px (CMake: ui_detach_panels_1440 at 100 %, ui_detach_panels_1440_200 at 200 %): the palette
# header's "Open in its own window" icon, the palette floating inside the window (offscreen: no window system to make
# an OS window), its header in the task menu while it's out, and Controls' own button. Every shot comes before the
# checks, so the script also shows an older build as it was.
logical_width 1440
run ui_look look=classic layout=classic
run new_sphere subdivisions=3
click "Tool##palette.tool"
hover "Tool/##detach"
wait 1.0
shot header-icon-tooltip
click "Tool/##detach"
wait 0.3
click "Display##tool.display"
wait 0.2
shot detached-floating
key f1
wait 0.3
shot controls-own-window-button
key escape
expect_value detached_panels == 1
